        <section id="tech-insights" class="py-20 mb-12 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="container mx-auto px-5 text-center">
                <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-center mb-10 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
                    <a href="index.html" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-bold mb-4 md:mb-0">
                        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-lg">arrow_back</span> Back to Home
                    </a>
                    <span class="text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider">Atlas Tech Insights</span>
                </div>

                <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-4 font-display">Tech Insights</h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-slate-400 max-w-3xl mx-auto">Latest analysis and research on AI security, compliance, and risk management</p>
                
                <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-400">
                    <span class="text-slate-400 self-center">On this page:</span>
                    <a href="#article-llm-red-teaming" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors bg-white/10 px-4 py-2 rounded-full shadow-sm border border-white/10 hover:border-primary text-slate-200">LLM Red Teaming</a>
                    <a href="#article-gdpr-agents" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors bg-white/10 px-4 py-2 rounded-full shadow-sm border border-white/10 hover:border-primary text-slate-200">GDPR Agents</a>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-16 text-left max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
                    
                    <!-- Article 1: LLM Red Teaming -->
                    <article id="article-llm-red-teaming" class="bg-slate-900/40 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-12 shadow-lg border border-white/10 scroll-mt-32 hover-card">
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-400 mb-6 uppercase tracking-wide">
                            <span class="text-primary bg-blue-50 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Red Teaming</span>
                            <span>May 15, 2024</span>
                            <span>•</span>
                            <span>5 min read</span>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold font-display text-white mb-6">The State of LLM Red Teaming 2024</h3>
                        <div class="prose prose-lg text-slate-300 max-w-none">
                            <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">Essential strategies for securing large language models against adversarial attacks and prompt injections in enterprise environments. As organizations race to adopt Generative AI, the attack surface expands significantly beyond traditional software vulnerabilities.</p>
                            <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Evolving Threat Landscape</h4>
                            <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">Traditional penetration testing methodologies fall short when dealing with the non-deterministic outputs of LLMs. Modern red teaming must now encompass prompt engineering, jailbreaking attempts, model extraction attacks, and training data poisoning.</p>
                            <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Strategic Mitigation</h4>
                            <p class="leading-relaxed">Implementing guardrails at both the input and output layers is crucial. This includes semantic analysis of prompts to detect malicious intent and verification of generated content against corporate safety policies before it reaches the end-user.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-white/10 flex justify-end">
                            <a href="#tech-insights" class="text-primary font-bold hover:text-primary-dark transition-colors flex items-center gap-2 text-sm">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-lg">arrow_upward</span> Back to top
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <!-- Article 2: GDPR Agents -->
                    <article id="article-gdpr-agents" class="bg-slate-900/40 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-12 shadow-lg border border-white/10 scroll-mt-32 hover-card">
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-400 mb-6 uppercase tracking-wide">
                            <span class="text-primary bg-blue-500/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Compliance</span>
                            <span>May 10, 2024</span>
                            <span>•</span>
                            <span>8 min read</span>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold font-display text-white mb-6">GDPR in the Age of Agents</h3>
                        <div class="prose prose-lg text-slate-300 max-w-none">
                            <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">How autonomous AI agents challenge current data privacy regulations and what legal teams need to prepare for. The shift from passive tools to active agents introduces new complexities in data controlling and processing roles.</p>
                            <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Autonomous Decision Making</h4>
                            <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">Under GDPR Article 22, individuals have the right not to be subject to a decision based solely on automated processing. AI agents that autonomously execute tasks—such as booking flights or managing finances—blur the lines of accountability and consent.</p>
                            <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Data Minimization Challenges</h4>
                            <p class="leading-relaxed">Agents often require vast context windows to function effectively. Ensuring these agents adhere to data minimization principles while maintaining performance requires a new architectural approach to memory management and context retrieval.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-white/10 flex justify-end">
                            <a href="#tech-insights" class="text-primary font-bold hover:text-primary-dark transition-colors flex items-center gap-2 text-sm">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-lg">arrow_upward</span> Back to top
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

